slides.append(slide(6,'4 · Manager Forecast Rollup','Managers own an evidence-based rollup; leadership inspects exceptions, not every CRM row',f'''
<div class="cadence"><div><b>MON</b><strong>Data hygiene</strong><span>AE updates stage, amount, close date, next step, business issue and contract timing.</span></div><div><b>TUE</b><strong>Manager inspection</strong><span>Remove weak deals, challenge slippage and confirm named forecast categories.</span></div><div><b>WED</b><strong>Team war room</strong><span>Only Stage 3+ deals that pass quality gates. Solve proof, stakeholder and timing gaps.</span></div><div><b>THU</b><strong>Executive rollup</strong><span>Managers submit commit, most likely, upside, risk, ICP mix and changes from last week.</span></div><div><b>FRI</b><strong>Action closure</strong><span>Owners close escalations; unresolved risks roll into next week with dates.</span></div></div>
<div class="grid-3">{card('War-room entry gate','ICP fit · quantified business issue · decision process · credible close date · scheduled next step.','QUALITY')}{card('Manager certification','Every forecasted deal is reviewed; any override includes written evidence and a date.','OWNERSHIP')}{card('Executive inspection','Focus on changes, gaps and asks. Leaders should not rebuild the manager forecast live.','CADENCE')}</div>
<div class="decision-banner"><b>Quality goal:</b> fewer deals in the room, more evidence per deal, and a forecast that changes only when buyer evidence changes.</div>'''))

